# folded_if_dead_clause_narrowing_ends -- The narrowing a dead clause's condition lays
# while it is checked ends with the clause: the else of a folded `if` still rules out
# what the code before the `if` ruled out, and so reads the one arm left.
shape: choice {
    circle: i64
    square: i64
    dot: null
}
SH: (shape.square 4)
main: function is {
    if SH.dot then return
    if SH.circle then print "circle" else print "else \{SH + 1}"
}
